## 🔥 RAGE ENGINE CORE CONCEPTS

### 1. **STREAMING ARCHITECTURE** (Most Important!)

**The Problem RAGE Solved:**
- GTA V map: 127 km² (49 square miles)
- Too large to fit in RAM
- Need seamless exploration (no loading screens)

**RAGE's Solution: Dynamic Streaming**

```
Player at position (X, Y):
  ↓
Load 500m radius around player
  ↓
Unload anything >1000m away
  ↓
Prioritize by:
  1. Distance (closer = higher priority)
  2. Direction (in front of camera = higher)
  3. Importance (mission area = highest)
  ↓
Stream from disk in chunks
```

**Our Implementation:**
```javascript
class WorldStreamer {
    constructor(scene, camera) {
        this.scene = scene;
        this.camera = camera;
        this.loadedChunks = new Map();
        this.chunkSize = 100; // 100m x 100m chunks
        this.loadRadius = 300; // Load within 300m
        this.unloadRadius = 500; // Unload beyond 500m
    }
    
    update() {
        const playerPos = this.camera.position;
        const playerChunk = this.getChunkCoords(playerPos);
        
        // Find chunks to load
        const chunksToLoad = this.getChunksInRadius(playerChunk, this.loadRadius);
        chunksToLoad.forEach(chunk => {
            if (!this.loadedChunks.has(chunk.id)) {
                this.loadChunk(chunk);
            }
        });
        
        // Find chunks to unload
        this.loadedChunks.forEach((mesh, chunkId) => {
            const chunkPos = this.getChunkPosition(chunkId);
            const distance = playerPos.distanceTo(chunkPos);
            if (distance > this.unloadRadius) {
                this.unloadChunk(chunkId);
            }
        });
    }
    
    async loadChunk(chunk) {
        // Load from server/disk
        const response = await fetch(`chunks/${chunk.id}.ply`);
        const geometry = await this.parsePLY(response);
        const mesh = new THREE.Points(geometry, this.material);
        mesh.position.set(chunk.x, 0, chunk.z);
        this.scene.add(mesh);
        this.loadedChunks.set(chunk.id, mesh);
    }
    
    unloadChunk(chunkId) {
        const mesh = this.loadedChunks.get(chunkId);
        this.scene.remove(mesh);
        mesh.geometry.dispose();
        this.loadedChunks.delete(chunkId);
    }
}
```

**Result:** Infinite worlds, constant 60 FPS!

