## 🔥 CORE PRINCIPLES (APPLY EVERYWHERE)

### 1. **NANITE** (Epic's Virtualized Geometry)

**The Core Concept:**
> "Only render triangles that are actually visible"

**Three Key Ideas:**

#### A) OCCLUSION CULLING
```
If player can't see it → Don't render it!

Example: Building behind another building
  Traditional: Render both (wasted GPU)
  Nanite: Check visibility, skip hidden one
  
Implementation:
  1. Frustum culling (not in camera view)
  2. Backface culling (facing away)
  3. Occlusion queries (blocked by other objects)
```

#### B) LOD CLUSTERING
```
Far away object = fewer triangles

Traditional LOD:
  Model_Full.obj (100K triangles)
  Model_Medium.obj (50K triangles)
  Model_Low.obj (10K triangles)
  Model_Billboard.png (1 quad)

Nanite LOD:
  • Generate LODs automatically
  • Blend seamlessly between levels
  • Per-triangle, not per-object
  • One asset, infinite detail levels
```

#### C) STREAMING
```
Don't load entire world → Load what's needed

Point Cloud Example (Your Warehouse):
  Total: 54M points (775 MB)
  
  Traditional: Load all 54M → OOM crash or 30s load
  
  Nanite-style:
    Load visible 2M points (30 MB) → 2s load
    Stream more as camera moves
    Unload what's behind
    Result: Instant, smooth
```

**How to Apply:**

**To Your Warehouse:**
```javascript
class NanitePointCloud {
    constructor(scene, camera) {
        this.scene = scene;
        this.camera = camera;
        this.visiblePoints = new Set();
        this.allPoints = []; // Chunked data
        this.maxVisiblePoints = 2000000; // 2M limit
    }
    
    update() {
        // 1. FRUSTUM CULLING
        const frustum = new THREE.Frustum();
        frustum.setFromProjectionMatrix(
            new THREE.Matrix4().multiplyMatrices(
                camera.projectionMatrix,
                camera.matrixWorldInverse
            )
        );
        
        // 2. DISTANCE CULLING
        const playerPos = this.camera.position;
        const maxDistance = 100; // 100m max
        
        // 3. LOD BY DISTANCE
        this.allPoints.forEach(chunk => {
            const distance = playerPos.distanceTo(chunk.center);
            
            // Not in frustum? Skip
            if (!frustum.intersectsBox(chunk.bounds)) return;
            
            // Too far? Skip
            if (distance > maxDistance) return;
            
            // Calculate LOD level
            let pointsToRender;
            if (distance < 20) {
                pointsToRender = chunk.points; // All points
            } else if (distance < 50) {
                pointsToRender = this.downsample(chunk.points, 0.5); // 50%
            } else {
                pointsToRender = this.downsample(chunk.points, 0.25); // 25%
            }
            
            // Render this chunk
            if (!this.visiblePoints.has(chunk.id)) {
                this.loadChunk(chunk, pointsToRender);
            }
        });
        
        // 4. UNLOAD INVISIBLE
        this.visiblePoints.forEach(chunkId => {
            const chunk = this.getChunk(chunkId);
            const distance = playerPos.distanceTo(chunk.center);
            
            if (distance > maxDistance * 1.5 || 
                !frustum.intersectsBox(chunk.bounds)) {
                this.unloadChunk(chunkId);
            }
        });
    }
}
```

